f23df13521393a577d237f7e5928c892cd43a55ca9d"}, {"path": "/home/mint/rl_dev/instinctRL-dev/tools/test_r6_decision.py", "sha256": "a2b9b7d7d2c30ffe0211f2e2b776a4c1f2a756fde70cc503bb619bda2db8179d"}, {"path": "/home/mint/.codex/sessions/2026/10/20/rollout-2026-10-20T00-06-59-01a154ea-8241-7dd3-aa33-41e485f17ca8.jsonl", "sha256": "222c3d0f6c0b76083d7641058d86931f16b573596f26e8198980f220ab3335df"}, {"path": "/home/mint/rl_dev/instinctRL-dev/docs/experiments/r6-robustness-auto/batch/calls/655b94d7271bec2c5e1b6132bebcff0bbb620170f49122caf77595acfd35fe01/events.jsonl", "sha256": "8e4d55ba4ef8a9bbc00362c8cb39699cc141fabd414c0dd8eef8d60899bc0d21"}, {"path": "/home/mint/rl_dev/instinctRL-dev/docs/experiments/r6-robustness-auto/batch/calls/badf0aab50e96ec4ec4a8c2aedc325d7f8e6dc8f09bacefcf79566456584ec75/events.jsonl", "sha256": "382ebe60b3f6d1b86d58c78d106035f0ebc4ac750efce7869036e82527f5542b"}], "notes": "Part A: reviewed ab1122f against 3078e95 and confirmed current repair source/tests equal ab1122f. The prior MUST_FIX is closed: complete_model_receipt checks event/request/process/exit identity and modern terminal cleanup, then records a fresh receipt and clears only its matching marker in one atomic Journal.save. Receipt replay repairs old split states without dispatch; other markers, later phases, receipt failure facts and reservations remain intact. Missing cleanup retains the active marker; failed decisions still raise after verified terminal cleanup. Inspected the actual save wrapper: it calls the durable save before injecting the exception when a receipt appears. Inspected the finalizer stale-marker regression and its single-call assertion. Hash-checked raw logs show both pre-repair failures, 57 initial passes and 61 final CPU passes; tests were not rerun. No new material defect found in this repair. Part B: all seven current pins checked; only r6_batch.py differs from review9. The unchanged validator's exact source comparison correctly invalidates the old approval with SOURCE_DRIFT; no approval was refreshed. A read-only attempted validator invocation could not complete because system Python lacks jsonschema, so this conclusion rests on inspected code and exact hash comparison, not a claimed successful validator run. Both original receipt/transcript/stderr/last-message bindings match, and read-only audit_event results exactly equal both original proposal rows. The exact supplement, raw 35-row session, six call/output record hashes and copied shell records match. The failed foreground cat attempt and metadata wrappers introduce no residual ownership ambiguity; listed capabilities were not invoked. Current process absence is supplementary only, never historical descendant-cleanup proof. The repair preserves the exact-two-receipt exception and strict modern cleanup enforcement. This reviewer must finish through its modern bounded worker receipt/usage/cleanup lifecycle before any later acceptance can consume this decision. No files, operational state or acceptance records were changed; no tests, GPU/simulator/model calls, subagents, background commands or installs were run. This grants no runtime dispatch, full-controller, capacity, protocol, production-snapshot compatibility or scientific acceptance.", "session_evidence": {"path": "/home/mint/rl_dev/instinctRL-dev/docs/experiments/r6-robustness-auto/LEGACY_MODEL_SESSION_SUPPLEMENT.json", "sha256": "75b2ccc8d85dd97dad666786b878ea30bc968bf24b0ac00a79353f7ae9bbedd6"}, "pipeline_repair_decision": "PASS_CPU_SCOPE", "pipeline_must_fix": []}
